listing:   run.sh (step nvme_trace) and boot.asm
toolchain: QEMU emulator version 8.2.2 (Debian 1:8.2.2+ds-0ubuntu1.18); NASM version 2.16.01
command:   qemu-system-x86_64 -machine q35 -nodefaults -display none -serial none -monitor none -no-reboot -drive file=.nvme.img,if=none,id=nv0,format=raw -device nvme,serial=HW205NVME,drive=nv0 -device isa-debug-exit,iobase=0xf4,iosize=0x04 -debugcon file:debugcon.txt -chardev file,id=fw,path=seabios.txt -device isa-debugcon,iobase=0x402,chardev=fw -trace 'pci_nvme_*' -D trace.txt
date:      2026-10-09T19:16:23Z
machine:   Linux x86_64 (cloud build container; QEMU with TCG, no KVM)
exit code: 33
hardware:  emulated NVMe controller only; untested on a physical SSD
note:      exit code 33 is expected: the boot sector wrote 0x10 to the isa-debug-exit port and QEMU exits with (0x10 << 1) | 1
